<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="ClypDat.App.Controls.ClypDatLoader"
             x:CompileBindings="False"
             Foreground="#FFFFFF">

  <!-- The app's loading mark, used wherever something is in flight: the startup
       loader, the clip-tile repair overlay, anywhere later.

       This is assets/clypdat-loader.svg, drawn with the SAME numbers: one
       304x304 space, the mark's own paths at the icon's own stroke widths
       (25 and 15, haloed at 33 and 21), and the ring at r=140 stroked 9 over a
       15 halo. Earlier versions here re-proportioned everything and stopped
       looking like the file they were supposed to be. If one changes, change
       both.

       The hexagons counter-rotate, and nothing else about them changes. That
       distinction is the whole trick to keeping it steady:

         - The mark is 180-degree symmetric - every vertex has an exact opposite
           - so a constant turn is smooth. What it is NOT is 60-degree
           symmetric: its sides alternate 103.94 and 102.00 units. Earlier
           versions turned it 0-60 per loop and it visibly snapped, so both
           rings here run a full 0-360.
         - SCALING is what actually wobbled. An earlier version breathed the
           inner hexagon between 0.88 and 1.04 and the mark looked like it was
           rocking. Nothing here scales except the glow, which has no edge to
           betray it.
         - Dashing the hexagons was the other failed idea: at tile size the
           dashes read as loose sticks rather than a hexagon. Dashes belong on
           the ring, which is a circle and holds its shape.

       The ring carries one segment per side of the mark - six - so it echoes
       the hexagon rather than contradicting it, and they tile the circumference
       exactly (146.608 x 6 = 879.65) so nothing snaps at the loop point. Note the one thing that
       cannot be copied between the two files verbatim: Avalonia measures
       StrokeDashArray in multiples of the stroke's own thickness, SVG measures
       stroke-dasharray in user units - so each pattern below is the SVG's
       divided by its own stroke width, and the halo's differs from the mark's.

       Vector throughout, so it is sharp at 24px and at 240px, and every stroke
       draws in Foreground so one property retints all of it. -->
  <Viewbox Stretch="Uniform">
    <Canvas Width="304" Height="304">

      <!-- Glow. The only thing that changes size. -->
      <Ellipse x:Name="Glow" Canvas.Left="22" Canvas.Top="22" Width="260" Height="260"
               Opacity="0.18">
        <Ellipse.Fill>
          <RadialGradientBrush>
            <GradientStop Offset="0" Color="#40FFFFFF" />
            <GradientStop Offset="1" Color="#00FFFFFF" />
          </RadialGradientBrush>
        </Ellipse.Fill>
      </Ellipse>

      <!-- Ring: SIX segments, one per side of the mark, so the ring echoes the
           hexagon instead of contradicting it. They tile the circumference
           exactly (146.608 x 6 = 879.65), so nothing snaps at the loop point.
           Halo and mark rotate as one Panel so they can never separate. r=140
           about the mark's centre, which is (152,152) here. -->
      <Panel x:Name="Ring" Canvas.Left="12" Canvas.Top="12" Width="280" Height="280">
        <Ellipse Width="280" Height="280"
                 Stroke="#000000" StrokeThickness="15"
                 StrokeDashArray="5.864,3.910" StrokeLineCap="Round"
                 Opacity="0.5" />
        <Ellipse Width="280" Height="280"
                 Stroke="{Binding $parent[UserControl].Foreground}" StrokeThickness="9"
                 StrokeDashArray="9.774,6.516" StrokeLineCap="Round"
                 Opacity="0.9" />
      </Panel>

      <!-- The mark, at the icon's own weights, offset by the same 24 units the
           SVG's viewBox is padded by. Each hexagon is its own layer so its halo
           turns with it. -->
      <Canvas Canvas.Left="24" Canvas.Top="24" Width="256" Height="256">
        <Canvas x:Name="OuterHexagon" Width="256" Height="256">
          <Path Data="M128 25 218 77v102l-90 52-90-52V77l90-52Z"
                Stroke="#000000" StrokeThickness="33" StrokeJoin="Round" Opacity="0.5" />
          <Path Data="M128 25 218 77v102l-90 52-90-52V77l90-52Z"
                Stroke="{Binding $parent[UserControl].Foreground}"
                StrokeThickness="25" StrokeJoin="Round" />
        </Canvas>
        <Canvas x:Name="InnerHexagon" Width="256" Height="256">
          <Path Data="m128 78 40 23v54l-40 23-40-23v-54l40-23Z"
                Stroke="#000000" StrokeThickness="21" StrokeJoin="Round" Opacity="0.5" />
          <Path Data="m128 78 40 23v54l-40 23-40-23v-54l40-23Z"
                Stroke="{Binding $parent[UserControl].Foreground}"
                StrokeThickness="15" StrokeJoin="Round" />
        </Canvas>
      </Canvas>
    </Canvas>
  </Viewbox>
</UserControl>
